#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119623 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "fe2f3934-fa5c-5a59-be7e-00b6e4889063" :question/math-academy-id "e-4810" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors $\\mathbf{b}_1$, $\\mathbf{b}_2$, $\\mathbf{b}_3$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\textrm{Null}(A)?$\n\n![](images/53/53e17b54ff077d45401bdc4754ccdcff5d0cad20e8d5b477b7a9e0aec37ab52c.svg)" :question/worked-solution "A vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ if $A\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{0}.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $\\mathbf{0}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-27 \\\\ 45 \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 40\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $\\mathbf{b}_2$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119624 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "e38db5fa-1753-5176-bb5e-a077ea63ddec" :question/math-academy-id "e-4812" :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](images/c8/c85268d7db6efb171da25432988c0ee99252f4cdb10f8a1cc24f31af5b2e239d.svg) and the vector ![](images/c7/c7095b22e7a8cbbeefc6b75b63886550a4c7c35f23585e2c0006ddf14b424c28.svg) Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Null}(A),$ then we must have $A\\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6+2k-12 \\\\ -6+3k-3 \\\\ 12-6k+6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2k-6=0 \\\\ 3k-9=0 \\\\ -6k+18=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119625 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "1e59cd29-ea54-5b90-8215-60c81d1b6dbb" :question/math-academy-id "e-4814" :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](images/17/17cd2f2b0846461e1ed6480f82ce576fc82e5066258d80ed6f7084b0d55ca4a9.svg) Find $\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that $x_2=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3(0) & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that ![](images/db/db533ede6312d49204e619379dfff639c0871f37ee997ce152ec35bd64105926.svg) is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\left\\{ \\mathbf{0} \\right\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ec9fb62-b74e-5f73-a9d7-24cdd8241f08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244733} {:answer/id #uuid "40c874be-9d6a-5355-9a2d-1de28e66c7fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244881} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0cb95e-5081-5fb0-b7e4-fccdc6b1560f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244990} {:answer/id #uuid "6477b993-602e-50ef-a5bf-f697d4de187f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245198} {:answer/id #uuid "d96b8ef7-018c-5dcb-aebd-a4407210a617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6477b993-602e-50ef-a5bf-f697d4de187f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245198} :answer-field/id #uuid "201f345b-15d4-533c-a4c9-80d020de8ac0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6241d446-37e4-5ee6-bee7-f843f3fd7347" :question/math-academy-id "q-111091" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}39 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-33 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, none of the vectors lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3522cb67-2a4c-5862-9742-5012bcf2a865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244787} {:answer/id #uuid "44acedda-ed58-5483-9469-72df6e1bec95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244918} {:answer/id #uuid "de936a6c-03fa-5da6-96aa-e7cb847a5ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246286} {:answer/id #uuid "df83aa96-d49e-5473-a388-8fb04d9a3f9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246297} {:answer/id #uuid "f2f1eafd-bc6e-5e24-b7ab-be5a1b1cd100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3522cb67-2a4c-5862-9742-5012bcf2a865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244787} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6098580-ef38-5be4-bc6d-471bd95ffa6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e9b223d-2f2b-5f4b-84d9-fe17b583795e" :question/math-academy-id "q-111112" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}28 & -7 & 14 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}28 & -7 & 14 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-7k+14 \\\\ k-2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-7k+14=0 \\\\ k-2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417740 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29619f9b-9f06-5558-89f7-4d0e65e0b6fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417712} {:answer/id #uuid "7d97603e-1f0e-5a8d-be4f-823054e6c132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417722} {:answer/id #uuid "8000a495-b4c4-55db-b5e6-b3a10f46cfdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417723} {:answer/id #uuid "88ca81a7-6293-5d02-80a7-1fbb2af96184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417724} {:answer/id #uuid "aa0d38bc-db7b-538c-b0be-911380152f0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29619f9b-9f06-5558-89f7-4d0e65e0b6fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417712} :answer-field/id #uuid "59767641-5ff1-522d-98ff-ca8331e026ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "87edb91a-a643-5fdb-a1df-2e5d059d6b9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-111154" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{2}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317454 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f81cf9e-4bfa-55eb-b6ae-699d514ced2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315482} {:answer/id #uuid "568d46fc-7170-5811-a4ce-5ea88b08b95f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315616} {:answer/id #uuid "60d73ea0-f6ad-5789-8e36-ce6055a05fe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315660} {:answer/id #uuid "98933544-bc80-5db2-a0ed-e7c7c59dfce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315969} {:answer/id #uuid "a08b61c7-baef-558c-ad66-db1d32e32bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f81cf9e-4bfa-55eb-b6ae-699d514ced2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315482} :answer-field/id #uuid "7741c95a-c056-57b4-9397-7a01a1ba8764" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "870e5cfd-95f3-5e52-b251-41fd48145e5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34392" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Null}(A)={0}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b313932-8a2d-5efe-9590-f6798ae0a9bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417709} {:answer/id #uuid "1839cd87-9807-5099-aa1b-8c59eca72147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417710} {:answer/id #uuid "4200484a-68ef-5a68-826c-3f22c3f6744b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417715} {:answer/id #uuid "43348635-a4e0-572f-b730-392f51070b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$,  ${b}_{2}$, and ${b}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417716} {:answer/id #uuid "aac34498-7b04-5d6d-ae12-08f353104028" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b313932-8a2d-5efe-9590-f6798ae0a9bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417709} :answer-field/id #uuid "e63daa46-8b3f-5be5-a899-eeb5be3faafc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "840cf185-0fde-50bc-83f8-78075677882d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74858" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the vectors lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$"}]}
